# Git must not rewrite line endings inside binary files.
#
# core.autocrlf is true in this clone, so without these rules Git treats an
# unrecognised file as text and converts LF to CRLF on checkout. For a PDF or an
# image that is corruption: the bytes change, the file no longer opens, and
# nothing warns you until somebody clones the repository and tries.
#
# Caught when adding IP/WanderForge-Interview-Prep.pdf, which Git reported as
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it".
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

# Text that must keep LF regardless of platform, because these are read by
# tooling and by Postgres rather than by a Windows editor.
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.js    text eol=lf
*.jsx   text eol=lf
*.mjs   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.css   text eol=lf
